# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Build output. Generated by `make build`; never commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build/ is hundreds of megabytes of object files, and install/ bakes in
# absolute paths from whichever machine last compiled it, so committing
# either produces a repository that is large AND broken on every other
# machine. `make build` recreates both in about ninety seconds.
build/
install/
log/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Local Python virtualenv
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Created by `make venv` for the one optional dependency (scipy), per the
# project rule against global pip installs. It is a local artefact: it holds
# absolute paths and platform-specific binaries.
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Python scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Results
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real trial data IS evidence and SHOULD be committed once a run is final --
# results/trials.csv and results/report.md are what the project's claims
# rest on, and a results table nobody can trace back to a CSV is not a
# result. The figures in results/figures/trials/ are drawn from that CSV
# and are committed with it. What is ignored here is only the throwaway
# output:
# (git only reads '#' as a comment at the START of a line: a comment after
#  a pattern becomes part of the pattern, and the pattern then matches
#  nothing. That is why these comments sit on their own lines.)
#
# synthetic, generated by `make verify`
results/demo_trials.csv
results/demo_report.md
results/figures/demo_trials/
# single-grasp demos from `make watch`
results/watch.csv
# the `make trials-quick` smoke test
results/quick.csv
results/quick_report.md
results/figures/quick/
results/scratch/
results/*.tmp.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Personal presentation notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# speech.txt is Kabir's own prep for the review: the spoken script, the facts
# to avoid misquoting, and anticipated viva questions. It is working material,
# not part of the deliverable, and there is no reason for it to be in the
# repository history.
speech.txt

# Editor noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
